+<a id="deepseek-aidsh-tool-macos-use"></a>
+
+## `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-macos-use`
+
+### `browser_click`
+
+Click the first element matching a CSS or Playwright text/role selector on the current page, e.g. "#submit" or 'text=Sign in'. Prefer this over browser_use_task for one known, selector-addressable click.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "selector": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "CSS or Playwright text/role selector."
+    }
+  },
+  "required": [
+    "selector"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts`](../packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts)
+
+### `browser_extract_text`
+
+Read the inner text of the first element matching a selector, or the whole page body when omitted.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "selector": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "CSS or Playwright selector; omitted = the whole page body."
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts`](../packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts)
+
+### `browser_fill`
+
+Replace the value of the first input matching a selector with literal text.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "selector": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "CSS or Playwright text/role selector for the input."
+    },
+    "text": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Text to set as the input's value."
+    }
+  },
+  "required": [
+    "selector",
+    "text"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts`](../packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts)
+
+### `browser_navigate`
+
+Navigate the automated browser tab to a URL, launching the browser first if needed.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "url": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Absolute URL to load."
+    }
+  },
+  "required": [
+    "url"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts`](../packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts)
+
+### `browser_screenshot`
+
+Capture a screenshot of the automated browser tab's current viewport and return it as an image.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {}
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts`](../packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts)
+
+### `browser_use_task`
+
+Autonomously operate the browser to accomplish a task: repeatedly screenshots the page, asks the configured GUI model where to click/type/press next, and executes that action, until the model reports the task done or the step budget runs out. Optionally navigates to a starting URL first. Use this for open-ended browsing tasks; prefer browser_navigate/browser_click/browser_fill/browser_extract_text when the exact selectors and steps are already known.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "task": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "The task to accomplish in the browser, in natural language."
+    },
+    "url": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Optional starting URL to navigate to before the loop begins."
+    },
+    "max_steps": {
+      "type": "integer",
+      "description": "Step budget from 1 to 100 before giving up. Defaults to 20 unless changed visually."
+    },
+    "postcondition": {
+      "type": "object",
+      "description": "Optional host-verified completion criteria. An empty object is rejected.",
+      "additionalProperties": false,
+      "properties": {
+        "url_equals": {
+          "type": "string",
+          "description": "Exact expected page URL."
+        },
+        "url_contains": {
+          "type": "string",
+          "description": "Case-sensitive substring required in the page URL."
+        },
+        "title_equals": {
+          "type": "string",
+          "description": "Exact expected page title."
+        },
+        "title_contains": {
+          "type": "string",
+          "description": "Case-sensitive substring required in the page title."
+        },
+        "text_contains": {
+          "type": "string",
+          "description": "Case-sensitive substring required in body or selector text."
+        },
+        "selector": {
+          "type": "string",
+          "description": "Selector that must resolve; text_contains applies to it when supplied."
+        }
+      }
+    }
+  },
+  "required": [
+    "task"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts`](../packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts)
+
+### `computer_abort`
+
+Immediately cancel active computer_use_task/browser_use_task calls owned by this same agent only. It cannot stop another agent; the visual Emergency Stop is explicitly global.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {}
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts`](../packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts)
+
+### `computer_click`
+
+Click, double-click, or right-click using either an opaque element token from computer_get_window_state or pixel coordinates from a fresh computer_screenshot.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "element": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Snapshot-scoped element token. Prefer this over coordinates."
+    },
+    "x": {
+      "type": "number",
+      "description": "Screenshot pixel x coordinate when element is omitted."
+    },
+    "y": {
+      "type": "number",
+      "description": "Screenshot pixel y coordinate when element is omitted."
+    },
+    "observation_id": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Required with x/y. One-action token returned by the immediately preceding computer_screenshot."
+    },
+    "button": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Defaults to \"left\".",
+      "enum": [
+        "left",
+        "right"
+      ]
+    },
+    "double_click": {
+      "type": "boolean",
+      "description": "Double-click instead of a single click. Ignored when button is \"right\"."
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts`](../packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts)
+
+### `computer_drag`
+
+Drag from a semantic element token or fresh screenshot pixel coordinate. With an element token, the destination is a global macOS point; with raw coordinates, it is a screenshot pixel. Heuristic human confirmation is on by default.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "element": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Snapshot-scoped token for the drag start."
+    },
+    "x": {
+      "type": "number",
+      "description": "Screenshot pixel start x when element is omitted."
+    },
+    "y": {
+      "type": "number",
+      "description": "Screenshot pixel start y when element is omitted."
+    },
+    "observation_id": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Required with x/y. One-action token returned by the immediately preceding computer_screenshot."
+    },
+    "to_x": {
+      "type": "number",
+      "description": "Global macOS point x with element; screenshot pixel x otherwise."
+    },
+    "to_y": {
+      "type": "number",
+      "description": "Global macOS point y with element; screenshot pixel y otherwise."
+    },
+    "duration_ms": {
+      "type": "integer",
+      "description": "Drag duration; defaults to 300ms."
+    }
+  },
+  "required": [
+    "to_x",
+    "to_y"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts`](../packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts)
+
+### `computer_focus_window`
+
+Bring one exact allowed macOS window to the front by id or app/title.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "window_id": {
+      "type": "integer",
+      "description": "CoreGraphics window id from computer_list_windows."
+    },
+    "app": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Application name when window_id is omitted."
+    },
+    "title": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Exact window title when selecting by app."
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts`](../packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts)
+
+### `computer_get_window_state`
+
+Capture one exact window and return its structured Accessibility controls with opaque tokens. Tokens become stale after the next snapshot or if the window moves/resizes.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "window_id": {
+      "type": "integer",
+      "description": "CoreGraphics window id from computer_list_windows."
+    },
+    "app": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Application name when window_id is omitted."
+    },
+    "title": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Exact window title when selecting by app."
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts`](../packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts)
+
+### `computer_key`
+
+Press a single key or modifier combo on macOS, e.g. "return", "escape", "cmd+shift+t", "a".
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "combo": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "Key or \"+\"-joined modifier combo."
+    },
+    "observation_id": {
+      "type": "string",
