+### `computer_use_task`
+
+Autonomously operate the macOS desktop to accomplish a task: repeatedly screenshots the screen, asks the configured GUI model where to click/type/press next, and executes that action, until the model reports the task done or the step budget runs out. Use this for open-ended desktop tasks; prefer the primitive computer_* tools for one specific, already-known action.
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "task": {
+      "type": "string",
+      "description": "The task to accomplish on the desktop, in natural language."
+    },
+    "max_steps": {
+      "type": "integer",
+      "description": "Step budget from 1 to 100 before giving up. Defaults to 20 unless changed visually."
+    },
+    "postcondition": {
+      "type": "object",
+      "description": "Optional host-verified completion criteria. An empty object is rejected.",
+      "additionalProperties": false,
+      "properties": {
+        "frontmost_app": {
+          "type": "string",
+          "description": "Expected frontmost application name (case/punctuation-insensitive)."
+        },
+        "frontmost_pid": {
+          "type": "integer",
+          "description": "Expected frontmost process id."
+        },
+        "window": {
+          "type": "object",
+          "description": "A visible window that must match every supplied field.",
+          "additionalProperties": false,
+          "properties": {
+            "id": {
+              "type": "integer"
+            },
+            "app": {
+              "type": "string"
+            },
+            "title": {
+              "type": "string"
+            },
+            "title_contains": {
+              "type": "string"
+            }
+          }
+        }
+      }
+    }
+  },
+  "required": [
+    "task"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Source: [`packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts`](../packages/macos-use/tool-macos-use/src/index.ts)
+
+Primitive desktop and browser tools execute directly against their capability seams. computer_use_task and browser_use_task call the separately configured GUI vision model once per step. Enabled step screenshots are durable tool-result metadata rendered only by the client; the driving model receives the textual task result.
+
